        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Treadmill packing comes down to stopping the heavy parts moving,
            protecting the console and its cable, and keeping every bolt with the machine.</strong>
            Lock and strap the deck, wrap or remove the console, bag and label the hardware, and use
            the original box if you have it or blankets, stretch wrap and corner protection if you
            do not.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Match the packing to the journey.</strong> A local move needs
            protection from knocks, storage needs protection from damp, and a return needs whatever
            the seller's policy says, so read it first. For the lifting and the stairs, our guide on
            <a href="/how-to-move-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">how to move a treadmill</a>
            picks up where this one ends.
